rtex that you disappeared into I think  anyone who who engages with the case  sort of goes down that that rabbit hole  because it's extraordinarily it's  fascinating it's incredible and it's  it's it's extraordinary an extraordinary  story and and horrifying horrifying that  it that it that it was still in fact you  know unfolding and and we wanted to do  what we could to assist I mean yeah  there was financial help but there was  also just an amazing knowledge and I  don't know where it comes from but she's  she just pulled everything together and  from that point on it just is it you  know I don't know how they did it they  were making films they were in the  middle of King Kong they they made  lovely bones they made all these films  and still managed to get Damien out of  prison so yeah you've always said we  always tell everyone this case is  nothing out of the ordinary this happens  all the time the only thing that made  ours different was that we were  fortunate enough to have cameras in the  courtroom that caught it on film there  are lots of people who aren't that lucky  you have people in Arkansas right now  you know people think that just because  you come up with DNA evidence or just  because people admit they lied on the  stand or just because new witness has  come forth people have this impression  that oh the case is over then he's going  to get out they're going to overturn it  and that's not true I mean that's only  fifty percent of the fight you can have  all the evidence in the world pointing  towards your innocence and they will  still kill you and sweep it under the  rug so that they don't have to admit  they made a mistake the other half of  the battle is getting word out to the  public letting people know what's going  on there were so many lies that we're  told in that courtroom and nothing made  any sense and then there were all these  people that actually were never even  in to testify like the alibi witnesses  it's just shocking you know ho